; a theory loaded in a `sandbox` is gone with it, and can be loaded again afterwards (in a proof
; block, `load` is not allowed: the loaded axioms would look proven there, like `use`)
sandbox
    load modal
    true
    summary
; `□` (modal.kurt's "necessarily") is gone too, not just its axioms -- a bare `□ true` is read as
; the undeclared constant `□` applied to `true`, with no rule to derive it
expect "ProofError" "`□` was never declared or used before"
    □ true
sandbox
    load modal    ; should be alright
    true
true

; and its symbols are gone with it: `⊢` is modal.kurt's prefix operator, a new symbol here
; (with modal.kurt still loaded, declaring it is an error)
prop ⊢
use ⊢
